Package: dragonfarm
Title: Fine-Tune Small Language Models with LoRA from R
Version: 0.3.4.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Tejas", "Patel", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "algocrat@gmail.com")
Description: Fine-tune small causal language models with LoRA (Low-Rank
    Adaptation) from R, and answer questions from your own documents.
    Documents (PDF, Word, HTML, Markdown, spreadsheets, web pages) are read
    into chunks, retrieved for each question, and answered from with cited
    sources; a model can write training questions from them for review.
    Tables of prompts and responses work too. Training runs in a background
    'Python' process built on Hugging Face 'transformers' and 'peft', with
    4-bit loading so a 7B model fits an 8 GB GPU, and a 'shiny' app covers
    the whole workflow. 'Python' dependencies are declared through
    'reticulate' and resolved automatically on first use.
